These endpoints send JSON errors with `Content-Type: text/plain`, so the content-type check misses them. Deciding based on the request's `responseType` covers that case. It also avoids parsing bodies axios has already decoded, which was CodeRabbit's point. Something like:

```ts
function buildErrorMessage(error: AxiosError): string {
  let data: unknown = error.response?.data;

  if (typeof data === "string" && error.config?.responseType === "text") {
    try {
      const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(data);
      if (parsed && typeof parsed === "object") data = parsed;
    } catch {
      // plain-text error body, keep as is
    }
  }

  return data ? extractErrorMessage(data, error.message) : error.message;
}
```

With this, you no longer need the header lookup.
